      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/fisharchive/pterodoras-granulosus-4/",
      "html": "<p>The Thorny Catfishes (Doradidae) are a small family of exclusively South American catfish. Currently 41 genera containing 127 species are known, but new species continue to be discovered. The largest species attain a maximum length of more than 100 cm. The world record for Opsodoras niger is 120 cm and a weight of 20 kg. The smallest species, Physopyxis lyra, becomes only 3.5 cm long. Most species attain a maximum length between 10 and 20 cm.</p><p>Pterodoras granulosus from Peru is a large species, which can become around 70 cm long. Juveniles of 7-10 cm were obtained.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/fisharchive/pterodoras-granulosus-4/",
      "html": "<p>This species is as peaceful as any species of thorny catfish, but one should keep in mind that the fish has a large mouth and smaller fish will vanish there of course.</p>"
    }
  ],
